se that they're able to connect  with and relate to just a really wide  array of fans  that also led to them being the first  k-pop girl group to perform at coachella  it would be a travesty to let lisa's day  go by without  doing a little dancing so my sister  micah and i are gonna try to learn  the kill this love dance which i  realized i can't show you with the music  because copyright you can see our  process and us trying to do the stance  over some nice  copyright royalty-free music well it is  the last day of our challenge  so today i'm just making a bunch of  foods that i've seen all the girls enjoy  together particularly in their show  in one of those episodes jenny wakes up  early to make all the girls pancakes  with fruit and all these  beautiful little toppings which i  thought was so sweet i am attempting to  make  japanese souffle pancakes as well you  don't make it fancy  but i know these are notoriously  difficult to make inga has a video up if  you want to follow her recipe who knows  how many times i'll need to try to make  these before they're right  despite my many failures they're well  worth the effort the texture is like out  of this world it's so fluffy  and light and the sweetness is so subtle  also makes me feel better that in black  pink house as  jen was making her pancakes she kept  flipping them wrong because that's  exactly what i did  you and me miss jenny both struggling  with our pancakes for lunch today i'm  making another dish that i've seen  blackpink cook together and that is  kimchi bokkeumbap or kimchi fried rice  they made it specifically with pork  belly and seasoned it with gochujang so  that's what i'm doing today  i decided to pair my kimchi book about  with a chun gochu just a  green chili pepper in the episode of  black pancas when they were eating this  rose was just munching on this pepper  and really often eaten with gochujang  just dipped in and eaten raw it's just  like a really yummy fresh way to break  up the  greasy heaviness of the fried rice  it is the final meal of our black pink  eating challenge but we're ending off  with a bang it's inspired by the episode  of blackpink house when they go to the  jinjibung which is just  a korean spa there's charcoal saunas  and you can get your body scrubbed down  but they also normally sell snacks  literally so relatable  they want to go have a spa day but were  so distracted by the snacks they had  sweet potatoes  dumplings tuck rice cakes noodles corn  all this stuff i'm not even gonna lie to  y'all this has probably been one of the  meals that i'm most excited for  in this whole week's challenge because  it's just 80 carbs i will say the only  part of this meal that i actually  cooked is the sauna eggs these eggs are  slow roasted  and they're really commonly served at  any korean spa  it's actually perfect to pair with my  tap goodie which is a combination of  chapagetti which is black bean noodles  and neo goodie which is a  seafood ramen brand in korea it got so  popular for people  to make the two together that now they  just manufacture like  bowls of chapo goodie which has the two  mixes mixed together for you  but in blackpink house rose was really  feeding in for some black bean noodles  so that's why i decided to get this  and before i get into dessert i wanted  to finish off this meal with our  blackpink fact  on spotify blackpink is the second most  streamed kpop artist after bts  making them the top most streamed kpop  girl group  reaching 300 million streams in 2020.  i didn't want to end off our last day  without a little of dessert i'm having  some [ __ ]  which rose was very enthusiastic about  getting at the kimchi bong it is a sweet  rice drink it's so refreshing and so  sweet and it has a little bit of a  grainy texture because there's actually  grains of rice like  floating around in there sadly as we're  at the end of our eating like blackpink  challenge  looking back in the photos trying to  figure out which day was my favorite  and i have to say i think the winning  day from this week was jesus  the juke and the chicken skewers the  shrimp were all  top-notch i would highly recommend  trying to make any of those dishes on  your own  as well as honestly anything from this  week was so delicious and so much fun so  i hope you all enjoyed and thank you so  much for watching and if there's any  other celebrity or group that you'd like  me to try to eat like please let me know  in the comments down below and i'll see  you in the next one  bye  you
 

